~ start
Sir Charles Smith II: Salutations Captain. [ID:charles 1.1]
You: Hey there Charles. Since you clean everyone's quarters so much, I was wondering if you've seen any signs of a possible mutiny on board? [ID:you 1.8]
Sir Charles Smith II: A mutiny? With this crew? I've never heard of such a thing! What a ridiculous presumption. What could possibly give you such an idea? [ID:charles 1.2]
You: So you really haven't seen or heard anything? [ID:you 1.9]
Sir Charles Smith II: Please Captain, if I had ever an inkling of a mutiny on this ship, you would have heard of it immediately. [ID:charles 1.3]
- Do you know where some of my gold could be? I have less than I did before?
	Sir Charles Smith II: Perhaps some of the other members took it. [ID:charles 1.4.1]
	You: Unless I'm mistaken, you are the only other member aboard with a key to my quarters. [ID:you 1.10.1]
	Sir Charles Smith II: Yes well, perhaps I misplaced my key. [ID:charles 1.5.1]
- Is there anyone you don't trust on this ship?
	You: Is there anyone you don't trust on this ship? [ID:you 1.10.2]
	Sir Charles Smith II: Mr. Mildred has always struck me as quite the... deceitful kind. On the other hand I have never known John to tell a lie. Quite a good fellow indeed. [ID:charles 1.4.2]
=> END